# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proprietary engineering drawings — NEVER commit these.
#
# Inputs/ holds customer manufacturing drawings (PDF + DWG). samples/ is the
# documented drop point for real drawings to audit locally (see samples/README).
# Both are confidential per CONSTITUTION §Security: uploaded documents stay on
# this machine. Only the checked-in README and the synthetic fixture generator
# are tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Inputs/
samples/*
!samples/README.md

# Generated test drawings — rebuilt by `python -m backend.demo.drawings samples/generated`
samples/generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAD files, wherever they land. A DWG or DXF in this repository is a customer
# drawing until proven otherwise, so they are ignored globally rather than only
# under Inputs/ — a file dropped in the project root is exactly how one leaks.
#
# The test suite needs no tracked CAD fixture: every DXF it reads is generated
# by ezdxf into a pytest temporary directory at run time. Should a checked-in
# fixture ever be needed, put it under tests/fixtures/cad/ and it is un-ignored
# below — that directory is for generated, non-proprietary files only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dwg
*.dxf
!tests/fixtures/cad/**

# PDFs are deliberately NOT ignored globally: the demo and regression drawings
# are synthetic PDFs the suite may need. The real ones live under Inputs/ and
# samples/, both ignored above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — NEVER commit. Checked by tests/test_secrets_hygiene.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.Python

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local audit output
audit*.png
audit*.json

# Validation harness output — overlays, JSON results and REPORT.md are
# regenerated from the drawings, and the drawings themselves are confidential.
validation/

# Golden production baselines (tools/baseline.py). Derived from customer drawings,
# which are not in this repository either, so the baselines are not committed.
# Keep them alongside the drawings; the tool that produces and checks them is
# tracked, which is the part that has to be reviewable.
baselines/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
